---
title: Creamy harissa butter beans
description: These creamy harissa butter beans take no time at all. Cook fresh butter beans or use canned and whip up the sauce in a matter of minutes for a simple and hearty main that can be eaten with bread, or veggies, or grains.
image: https://plantbasednews.org/app/uploads/2026/05/creamy-harissa-butter-beans.jpg
source: https://plantbasednews.org/veganrecipes/dinner/creamy-harissa-butter-beans/#recipe
course: Dinner
cuisine: Vegan
tags: butter beans, creamy, harissa, sun-dried tomato
servings: 2
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
---

Chop the @onion{1}(chopped) and @sun-dried tomatoes{6}(chopped) and grate the @garlic{1%clove}(minced).

In a wide #pan{} on medium heat, add the @sun-dried tomato oil{2%tbsp} or @olive oil{} and the onion along with a pinch of @salt{} and sauté for ~{5%minutes} until translucent.

Then add the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes and sauté for ~{1%minutes} before you add the @harissa paste{1%tsp}.

Stir it in for a minute, then add the @water{150%ml} bit by bit.

Continue with the @butter beans{450%g} and a generous pinch of @salt{} and @ground black pepper{} and stir everything well to combine.

Add the @soya cooking cream{250%g} and cook for ~{2%minutes}.

Lastly finish it with the @fresh spinach{50%g} and cook for a further ~{2%minutes} until just wilted.

> Serve with your favorite bread.
